cff-version: "1.2.0"
title: "globalPCD — Passive cavitation detection prototype toolkit"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cronin
    given-names: Siobhan K
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SioKCronin/globalPCD"
abstract: >-
  Python toolkit that emits a versioned PCDReading (cavitation regime,
  confidence, optional location, latency) for focused-ultrasound controllers.
  Designed for holding sonications in the stable-cavitation window
  (research-only); synthetic PCD and optional array localization are
  included.
keywords:
  - passive cavitation detection
  - focused ultrasound
  - stable cavitation
  - neuromodulation
  - histotripsy
  - ultrasound
  - beamforming
version: "0.1.1"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
